    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0359" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/5939: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-20T00:00:00-04:00">August 20,
                            1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3964. Reference Department’s 3568, July 30, 1942. Stockholm informs us that
                    guarantee with respect to limitation on Swedish extension of credit to Germany
                    may be impossible to obtain. We emphasize that the military concessions are the
                    concessions most to be desired. We are anxious to know how negotiations are
                    progressing.</p>
                <p>For your information we repeat telegram to Stockholm.</p>
                <p>(Quote telegram to Stockholm.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d311-f1"/>)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
